---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';

// If marketing tags (Meta Pixel, Google Ads) are ever added, they need a consent banner first (PECR), and this page needs updating.
---

<Legal
  title="Cookies"
  description={`${site.name} uses no advertising or tracking cookies. Here is what is stored in your browser and why.`}
  updated="2026-10-27"
  intro="We don't use advertising or tracking cookies, so there's no cookie banner. The only things stored in your browser are needed to take a booking safely."
>
  <h2>What is stored, and why</h2>
  <div class="table">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th scope="col">Name</th><th scope="col">Set by</th><th scope="col">What for</th><th scope="col">How long</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>__stripe_mid, __stripe_sid</td>
          <td>Stripe</td>
          <td>Fraud prevention on the payment step. Only set on the checkout page when you pay by card.</td>
          <td>1 year and 30 minutes</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>__cf_bm</td>
          <td>Cloudflare</td>
          <td>Telling people from bots, to protect the site. Only set if Cloudflare's bot protection is triggered.</td>
          <td>30 minutes</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>booking:[reference]</td>
          <td>This site (session storage, not a cookie)</td>
          <td>Shows your booking summary on the confirmation page after you book.</td>
          <td>Until you close the tab</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    Our contact and enquiry forms are checked for spam by Cloudflare Turnstile, which runs a short check in your browser. Cloudflare uses
    what it collects only for that check.
  </p>
  <p>
    These are all strictly necessary for the site to work securely, so the law doesn't require us to ask first. You can still block or
    delete them in your browser settings, but paying for a booking may not work if you do.
  </p>

  <h2>Counting visits</h2>
  <p>
    We see how many people visit and which pages they read through Cloudflare Web Analytics. It doesn't use cookies, doesn't store
    anything on your device and doesn't follow you across other websites.
  </p>

  <h2>If this changes</h2>
  <p>
    If we ever add cookies that aren't strictly necessary, such as for advertising, we'll ask for your permission first and update this
    page. Our <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> covers how we use personal information more generally.
  </p>
</Legal>
